  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 AM CDT Sat May 30 2026\n\nDrier conditions will prevail over South Texas through the early \npart of next week thanks to ridging aloft. Warmer conditions will \nalso exist through this period with highs in the 80s and 90s across \nthe region with heat indices around 100-105. This will also prevail \nthrough the next week. This will lead to minor to moderate heat \nstress conditions. \n\nThe chances for showers and storms will return to the region next \nweek as the ridge weakens allowing for some shortwave energy to \ncreep into the region which will combine with the seabreeze. This \nwill be coupled with a surge of moisture thanks to the return of \nonshore flow Sunday evening. A low to medium chance for showers and \nthunderstorms will exist everyday of next week beginning Monday. The \nhighest chances for rainfall will be in the afternoon and tapering \noff in the evening with the loss of daytime heating.",
